error_signature: "TypeError: CMake.build() got an unexpected keyword argument 'args'"
root_cause: "Conan 2.x CMake.build() has no 'args' parameter; its signature is build(build_type, target, cli_args, build_tool_args, stdout, stderr, subfolder). Recipes migrated from autotools-style intuition call cmake.build(args=['-j1']) which raises TypeError. Tool args (e.g. -j1 for make) must go through build_tool_args; cmake --build args through cli_args."
rec_approach: "cmake-build-build-tool-args"
match_keywords: ["TypeError", "CMake.build", "unexpected keyword argument", "args", "build_tool_args", "cli_args"]
error_excerpt: "ERROR: libcorrect/3.5@ohpcd/stable: Error in build() method\n\tcmake.build(args=[\"-j1\"])\n\tTypeError: CMake.build() got an unexpected keyword argument 'args'"
severity: P1
category: conan, cmake, recipe
last_updated: 2026-09-27
similar_to: ["E426"]
boundary_novelty: "E426 and DRAFT-zmusic use build_tool_args correctly but never record the args= TypeError error surface; this entry captures the migration error for recipes that reach for args=."